14
01:13:40.834 --> 01:13:43.834
And that we may look more and more to Jesus. Amen.

15
01:13:44.834 --> 01:13:50.834
And today, on this last Sunday, I also want to present a word to us.

16
01:13:50.834 --> 01:13:56.834
And that word is also characteristic when it comes to the subject of gratitude.

17
01:13:56.834 --> 01:14:04.834
For it is good to pause in gratitude at certain moments.

18
01:14:04.834 --> 01:14:12.834
Throughout humanity, through history, you see that every time there is a festival or a celebration...

19
01:14:12.834 --> 01:14:17.834
these are often milestones where we reflect on what happened.

20
01:14:17.834 --> 01:14:20.834
Just think of your birthday for example.

21
01:14:20.834 --> 01:14:23.834
Nowhere in the Bible does it say that you must celebrate your birthday.

22
01:14:23.834 --> 01:14:30.834
Only every time you celebrate your birthday to celebrate that you were born, that you live in this world.

23
01:14:30.834 --> 01:14:36.834
And it is good and it is nice to pause in gratitude for what your birthday is.

24
01:14:36.834 --> 01:14:42.834
In the same way, we see a few weeks ago that, for example, the Jewish festival of Hanukkah was celebrated.

25
01:14:42.834 --> 01:14:45.834
And that is not necessarily commanded by God in the Bible.

26
01:14:45.834 --> 01:14:52.834
Only there is an event that happens in history and the Jewish people pause to celebrate that.

27
01:14:52.834 --> 01:14:56.834
You also had the Feast of Harvest and the Feast of Tabernacles.

28
01:14:56.834 --> 01:15:00.834
Which was indeed revealed by God that it should be celebrated.

29
01:15:00.834 --> 01:15:09.834
The Feast of Tabernacles was a feast in which it was celebrated that the people of Israel were freed from captivity in Egypt.

30
01:15:09.834 --> 01:15:12.834
And that they ultimately come to stand in that freedom.

31
01:15:12.834 --> 01:15:17.834
And the Feast of Tabernacles is then a feast to pause in gratitude.

32
01:15:17.834 --> 01:15:25.834
So all kinds of milestone situations should actually function to make you pause.

33
01:15:25.834 --> 01:15:30.834
And to remember, and here comes my teaching for today, who God is.

34
01:15:30.834 --> 01:15:32.834
That's what it's about.

35
01:15:32.834 --> 01:15:37.834
The best thing you can do, and that's what my teaching is about today.

36
01:15:37.834 --> 01:15:46.834
The best thing you can do is always think in gratitude about who God is.

37
01:15:46.834 --> 01:15:48.834
Right?

38
01:15:48.834 --> 01:15:52.834
And so also when we stand at the end of this year, you can actually...

39
01:15:52.834 --> 01:15:56.834
And this is also what we just heard during the prayers.

40
