42
01:16:03.834 --> 01:16:15.834
You just heard in my prayer, and also in the various prayers, that the ingredients of gratitude are often filled with...

43
01:16:15.834 --> 01:16:21.834
Thank you for giving me a wonderful family.

44
01:16:21.834 --> 01:16:26.834
So thank you, I just prayed, thank you for my dear wife, and for my dear children.

45
01:16:26.834 --> 01:16:30.834
Thank you for health, thank you that you continue to work in me.

46
01:16:30.834 --> 01:16:32.834
And that can be turned off.

47
01:16:32.834 --> 01:16:35.834
And that can be turned off, and that can be turned off.

48
01:16:35.834 --> 01:16:37.834
I'm joking, Robert.

49
01:16:37.834 --> 01:16:39.834
Robert is gaming.

50
01:16:39.834 --> 01:16:41.834
But...

51
01:16:41.834 --> 01:16:44.834
That would be something, right?

52
01:16:45.834 --> 01:16:51.834
Okay, so prayers and gratitude are good...

53
01:16:51.834 --> 01:16:53.834
Listen carefully to what I am saying.

54
01:16:53.834 --> 01:16:58.834
And not later, when I make a comparison, think that one was not good.

55
01:16:58.834 --> 01:17:00.834
It is really very human to do this.

56
01:17:00.834 --> 01:17:09.834
It is good to approach God in gratitude for the things you see happening in your life.

57
01:17:09.834 --> 01:17:12.834
That is good. Gratitude is good.

58
01:17:12.834 --> 01:17:20.834
When we give Joshua and Olivia gifts at Christmas, we as educating parents afterwards force them to...

59
01:17:20.834 --> 01:17:24.834
Then we say to them, hey, thank you.

60
01:17:24.834 --> 01:17:27.834
That's nice, right? When you receive something, thank you.

61
01:17:27.834 --> 01:17:34.834
And so it is human and it is good to be grateful for the things that happen in your life.

62
01:17:34.834 --> 01:17:35.834
Amen?

63
01:17:35.834 --> 01:17:38.834
It is good to be grateful for your health.

64
01:17:38.834 --> 01:17:41.834
It is good to be grateful, and I do that one last time...

65
01:17:41.834 --> 01:17:50.834
In the last year, I have increasingly paused in my prayer, for example before meals, to take a moment of silence...

66
01:17:50.834 --> 01:18:00.834
and to realize that it is not normal to have daily food and so much choice...

67
01:18:00.834 --> 01:18:04.834
that you walk into a supermarket where, I don't know, 50,000 items are available...

68
01:18:04.834 --> 01:18:09.834
and that you almost get choice stress about what should I eat tonight.

69
01:18:09.834 --> 01:18:11.834
Because there is so much available.

70
01:18:11.834 --> 01:18:16.834
And we, people of the Western world, we might think and say that...

71
01:18:16.834 --> 01:18:18.834
you can take that for granted.

72
01:18:18.834 --> 01:18:23.834
Or you can pause in gratitude towards God...

73
01:18:23.834 --> 01:18:27.834
and express a prayer of thanks and say, thank you, Lord...

74
01:18:27.834 --> 01:18:31.834
that I have never been hungry in 2025.

75
01:18:31.834 --> 01:18:37.834
And that can lead you to a prayer that you can pray about world poverty.

76
01:18:38.834 --> 01:18:41.834
Yes, can I pray for world poverty? Yes!

77
01:18:41.834 --> 01:18:46.834
Because it is not based on your authority, but it is based on the authority of Jesus.

78
01:18:46.834 --> 01:18:52.834
So your prayer, in the name of Jesus, you can pray against world poverty.

79
01:18:52.834 --> 01:18:54.834
You can pray against wars.

80
01:18:54.834 --> 01:18:56.834
Do you understand what I mean?

81
01:18:56.834 --> 01:19:01.834
So it is good to pause and reflect on personal testimonies.

82
01:19:01.834 --> 01:19:05.834
It is good to pause and reflect on personal thanksgivings.

83
01:19:05.834 --> 01:19:08.834
It is good to pause and reflect on your salvation.

84
01:19:08.834 --> 01:19:12.834
It is good to pause and reflect on you, and so on, and so forth.

85
01:19:12.834 --> 01:19:16.834
The only word that I want to teach you today is a word...

86
01:19:16.834 --> 01:19:20.834
I just had to briefly check with Marco whether that is actually a Dutch word?

87
01:19:20.834 --> 01:19:22.834
But I just took the English word with me.

88
01:19:22.834 --> 01:19:26.834
Because that is how I learned it in my training.

89
01:19:26.834 --> 01:19:30.834
And that is the word, I made a picture of it with ChattyPT.

90
01:19:31.834 --> 01:19:36.834
And the word I want to teach you today is the word doxology.

91
01:19:36.834 --> 01:19:42.834
And the word doxology is a word that does not center itself...

92
01:19:42.834 --> 01:19:48.834
on your gratitude towards God for the things that God does in your life.

93
01:19:48.834 --> 01:19:53.834
But doxology is a word that centers itself on who God is.

94
01:19:53.834 --> 01:19:57.834
And that your gratitude is based on that.

95
01:19:57.834 --> 01:20:00.834
So doxology is a word...

96
01:20:00.834 --> 01:20:07.834
You see in the word doxology, there is the Greek word doxa and logie.

97
01:20:07.834 --> 01:20:12.834
So I asked Marco, is doxology for example a good Dutch word?

98
01:20:12.834 --> 01:20:17.834
Yes, it can be. But doxology is...

99
01:20:17.834 --> 01:20:21.834
Logie means word, comes from logos, and doxa means glory.

100
01:20:22.834 --> 01:20:26.834
So the word you see here is glory word.

101
01:20:26.834 --> 01:20:29.834
Or better said, thanksgiving.

102
01:20:29.834 --> 01:20:34.834
Keeping yourself occupied with thanksgiving.

103
01:20:34.834 --> 01:20:41.834
But when we say the word doxology in our Christian language, or doxologie then...

104
01:20:41.834 --> 01:20:47.834
it always has to do with the fact that you keep yourself occupied...

105
01:20:47.834 --> 01:20:53.834
and here comes what I just said, it is good to express your gratitude towards God...

106
01:20:53.834 --> 01:20:59.834
that you are healthy, that you have a good career, that you have a nice marriage...

107
01:20:59.834 --> 01:21:02.834
and that things are going well for you and that you are saved in the name of Jesus.

108
01:21:02.834 --> 01:21:05.834
That is good. But doxology is even better.

109
01:21:05.834 --> 01:21:09.834
For doxology says that He is great.

110
01:21:09.834 --> 01:21:12.834
That He is king. That God is eternal.

111
01:21:12.834 --> 01:21:16.834
That God is powerful. That He is true.

112
01:21:16.834 --> 01:21:18.834
That He is just.

113
01:21:18.834 --> 01:21:23.834
That He has been and that He still is and that He will come.

114
01:21:23.834 --> 01:21:25.834
That He is the beginning and the end.

115
01:21:25.834 --> 01:21:28.834
That He comes on a white horse. That He will return.

116
01:21:28.834 --> 01:21:30.834
That He has come and will come again.

117
01:21:30.834 --> 01:21:32.834
That He is Savior and Lord.

118
01:21:32.834 --> 01:21:40.834
And if you fill your life with doxology, if you fill your life with gratitude...

119
01:21:40.834 --> 01:21:48.834
about who He is, Christ-centered, in contrast to ego-centered...

120
01:21:48.834 --> 01:21:54.834
egocentric, Christian-centric, Christ-centered...

121
01:21:54.834 --> 01:21:57.834
So, here is my tip that I want to give you...

122
01:21:57.834 --> 01:22:02.834
if you fill your life in 2026...

123
01:22:03.834 --> 01:22:07.834
then you will fill your life the best...

124
01:22:07.834 --> 01:22:11.834
with as much God-centered gratitude as possible.

125
01:22:13.834 --> 01:22:16.834
Well, Paul, we have been studying the letter to the Ephesians...

126
01:22:16.834 --> 01:22:20.834
in the past two months we have covered the letter to the Ephesians and the letter to the Philippians...

127
01:22:20.834 --> 01:22:25.834
and I want to show you how Paul does this in the letters to the Ephesians and Philippians.

128
01:22:25.834 --> 01:22:33.834
Because I have taken two doxologies from the letter to the Ephesians and the letter to the Philippians.

129
01:22:33.834 --> 01:22:36.834
I have taken two pieces where Paul...

130
01:22:36.834 --> 01:22:39.834
and that is why I have taken the HSV translation...

131
01:22:39.834 --> 01:22:44.834
because the HSV translation is closest to the Greek translation...

132
01:22:44.834 --> 01:22:50.834
and one of the characteristics of a doxology is that...

133
01:22:50.834 --> 01:22:53.834
one, what I just said, it is God-oriented...

134
01:22:53.834 --> 01:22:56.834
two, it goes in one go from...

135
01:22:56.834 --> 01:22:59.834
and you see Paul doing this in the letter to the Ephesians...

136
01:22:59.834 --> 01:23:02.834
and you see Paul doing it in the letter to the Philippians as well...

137
01:23:02.834 --> 01:23:05.834
he starts right away with a greeting...

138
01:23:05.834 --> 01:23:08.834
Hello Open Church, it is nice to be here...

139
01:23:08.834 --> 01:23:11.834
really great to see all of you again...

140
01:23:11.834 --> 01:23:15.834
and all at once, and that is a bit technical in language...

141
01:23:15.834 --> 01:23:18.834
Nani, maybe if you could go to the next picture...

142
01:23:18.834 --> 01:23:23.834
In one glance, you see in this jumble of words...

143
01:23:23.834 --> 01:23:26.834
